      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(elevenlabs): validate baseUrl with user-friendly error for malformed endpoints (fixes #106943)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nnormalizeElevenLabsBaseUrl only trimmed whitespace and stripped trailing slashes — zero URL validation. A malformed baseUrl produces a raw TypeError from new URL() deeper in the call chain. The realtime provider also did not accept ws/wss for direct WebSocket endpoints.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwo independent normalizers with scoped scheme validation, following the Deepgram pattern from #105334:\n- normalizeElevenLabsBaseUrl (shared): validates http/https for API callers\n- normalizeElevenLabsRealtimeBaseUrl (realtime): validates http/https/ws/wss for WebSocket transport\n\nThe realtime URL builder constructs URLs via pathname join, mapping http→ws and https→wss while preserving direct ws/wss endpoints.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMalformed ElevenLabs baseUrl values produce a clear error. Self-hosted WebSocket endpoints are supported. Valid URLs are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\nLocal test run: 5 test files, 37 tests passed.\n\n- shared.ts — URL parse + http/https scheme validation\n- realtime-transcription-provider.ts — independent realtime normalizer accepting ws/wss\n- shared.test.ts — 10 cases for the shared normalizer",
        "branch": "fix/issue-106943-elevenlabs-baseurl-validate",
